{"videoId":"S6uienJsj4s","title":"SHADING explained in 5 minutes","author":"Zumikito Miniatures","authorId":"UChvLrvN9TyZ-rCuxPIhUHiA","published":1613689200000,"description":"Shading miniatures adds more contrast to them and makes them more readable. Using a wash might be a good idea, but is there a way to shade your miniatures more easily? Today, we will also mention speedpainting methods for warhammer.\n\nToday's sponsor is Shieldwolf Miniatures: https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/shieldwolf/imperium-desertum-imperium-immortalis?ref=profile_created\n\nHave you ever wondered if there is a way that could be easier than washing your miniature to shade it? Well, using a wash to stack shades in the recesses might be effective when it comes to painting fur, bases, terrain and other stuff with a plenty of texture, but what about that flat armor? Space marines and tanks certainly don't enjoy full washes. Recess shading might be one of your options, but using oil wash or enamel wash for panel lining is also a great idea! Using washes like these will make them go straight into recesses, effectively panel lining your miniature.\n\nCertainly, when I finally paint the entire half of my space marine indomitus box, I will use one of the faster panel lining methods mentioned instead of recess shading.\n\nThese videos are essential watch if you want to improve:\nPainting Volumes: https://youtu.be/mw4NcKqaPJ0\nPainting Non Metallic Metal: https://youtu.be/wOGlHTRySlU\n\nThese hobby tools are a MUST if you wanna improve: https://youtu.be/UqgElHtomVw \n\nSupport the channel by purchasing any hobby products using following links (As an Amazon Associate I earn from qualifying purchases you do after using these links at no extra cost for you)\n\nAmazon US:\nAny product: https://amzn.to/37GMBGT\nI use Panasonic GH5 camera: https://amzn.to/3qNOTLP\nBasic Vallejo Colors: https://amzn.to/3pJd2BI\nLAMP: https://amzn.to/3s7wiuK \nVallejo Texture Paste: https://amzn.to/3CiHA4M\nWinsor and Newton series 7 brush: https://amzn.to/3yshutO\nStarting airbrush set: https://amzn.to/3s8NhwI\n\nAmazon UK:\nAny product: https://amzn.to/3wGfBK3\nI use Panasonic GH5 camera: https://amzn.to/30aZVCX\nBasic Vallejo paints: https://amzn.to/30fybNn\nLAMP: https://amzn.to/3og7T5J\nStarting airbrush set: https://amzn.to/2YzNDTD\n\nAmazon DE (and EU):\nAny product: https://amzn.to/392bXzs\nI use Panasonic GH5 camera: https://amzn.to/3w30DNJ\nBasic Vallejo paints: https://amzn.to/3cdUmH0\nLAMP: https://amzn.to/37hqAh1 \nStarting airbrush set: https://amzn.to/39h2CUT\n\nI use 3D printer from Anycubic: https://bit.ly/3akLGfP\n\nAll the music and soundeffects are from Epidemic Sound, support the channel by registering via this link: https://www.epidemicsound.com/referral/npn6j7/\n\nhttps://www.facebook.com/zumikit0/\nhttps://www.instagram.com/zumikit0/\n\nI am painting miniatures for warhammer, age of sigmar, marvel crisis protocol, D&D and much more! Whether it is superhero miniatures, heroic characters or space marines, I will paint them! If you are looking for some sweet miniature painting tutorials or warhammer hobby content in general, this is the right channel for you!","viewCount":138022,"lengthSeconds":327,"watchProgress":320.259202,"timeWatched":1681372988903,"isLive":false,"paid":false,"type":"video","_id":"2mPEouVmXLvRjN6V"}
