{"videoId":"dDdGCbCc5Kw","title":"Sanda Single Leg Takedown","author":"kungfukulture","authorId":"UCSKFM9gmsHVwr_uPFOjruQQ","published":1606262400000,"description":"The International Wushu Federation launches an Online Wushu Classroom Project on May 15, 2020, free of charge to all global wushu practitioners and the general public. We hope these courses will bring a boost of physical and mental health to wushu enthusiasts around the world. \n\nThe classes are often scheduled at 10am or 3pm Beijing Time, several on 6pm. LIVE classes will be delivered at ZOOM and YouTube (@WushuTV); Recorded classes will be available on YouTube and Tencent video. All replay or video recordings will be updated on IWUF official website and social media channels.\n\nDemonstrators: Guoshun SHEN, Hongxing KONG\n                             World Wushu Sanda Champions\nAdvisor: Shiying LI \n\nHow To Join from Zoom: (Click https://us02web.zoom.us/j/7376379510 to download Zoom app, input Zoom ID: 7376379510, and you will enter the LIVE Zoom platform to interact with great wushu teachers; No registration or password needed.)\nYouTube: https://www.youtube.com/user/iwufwushu\n\nVisit http://www.iwuf.org/news/ for classroom schedules.\n\nSUBSCRIBE to our channels for classes replay or video recordings. \nIWUF Official Website: http://www.iwuf.org/multimedia/wushu-tv/\nYouTube: https://www.youtube.com/user/iwufwushu\nTencent Video: https://v.qq.com/s/videoplus/507535140\n\nLIKE us on Facebook: @iwufofficial (https://www.facebook.com/iwufofficial)  \nFOLLOW us on Twitter, Instagram, Douyin, Weibo and WeChat. \nTwitter: @iwufofficial (www.twitter.com/iwufofficial) \nInstagram:@iwuf_official @iwufnews (www.instagram.com/iwuf_official) \nWeibo: https://www.weibo.com/iwuf\nDouyin: IWUF_official (@国际武联IWUF)\nWeChat: IWUF official (@国际武术联合会IWUF)","viewCount":1475,"lengthSeconds":158,"watchProgress":125.122978,"timeWatched":1707149044355,"isLive":false,"type":"video","_id":"YWRpg4k7VAFmc21M"}
{"videoId":"2xC45pBXAV0","title":"Transferring Games Workshop/Citadel Paint From Pots to Bottles | Tutorial","author":"Sleepy WhatsIt","authorId":"UC-mR0DRC2i1VwT3sjgaZaYA","published":1595628000000,"description":"This video covers the process that I use for transferring Games Workshop/Citadel paints from their original paints pots to dropper bottles.\n\n#MiniaturePainting #GamesWorkshop #HowTo\n\nThe entire process is shown step by step, including discussing the tools and products I use, along with helpfulp tips to make things easier. I also explain the reasoning behind why I transferred my paints, so that you can decide if this is right for you.\n\nTimestamps for the video\n0:00 - Cold Open\n0:22 - Introduction\n1:50 - Process\n10:49 - Conclusion\n\nIf you want to support the channel directly, you can through: https://ko-fi.com/sleepywhatsit\n\nI have removed the Amazon links that used to be here, since I left their affiliate program over a dispute related to payment.\n\nContact:\n  contact at sleepywhatsit dot com\n  Instagram:  https://www.instagram.com/sleepywhatsit/\n  Tumblr:  https://www.tumblr.com/sleepywhatsit\n  Ko-Fi:  https://ko-fi.com/sleepywhatsit\n  Twitch:  https://twitch.tv/SleepyWhatsIt\n\nCredits:\n  \"Baba Yaga\" Kevin MacLeod (incompetech.com)\n  Licensed under Creative Commons: By Attribution 3.0 License\n  http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0/","viewCount":18382,"lengthSeconds":726,"watchProgress":129.712875,"timeWatched":1682695904704,"isLive":false,"paid":false,"type":"video","_id":"YY2J0UKYiuOq7nAD"}
