{"videoId":"x0Kbj4lEOag","title":"Some Context on Docker Contexts","author":"Docker","authorId":"UC76AVf2JkrwjxNKMuPpscHQ","published":1639609200000,"description":"Did you miss the Docker Community All-Hands on December 9, 2021? \n\nHere is a replay of the talk hosted by Jacob Howard (@xenoscopic): Some Context on Docker Contexts.\n\nDocker Contexts make working with multiple Docker Engines faster and less tedious. They're also super easy to use and understand, so in just a few minutes you'll be able to fully integrate them into your Docker-based workflows.\n\nJoin our community on Slack: https://bit.ly/3Em3zsi\n\nYou can follow Docker on social networks:\nTwitter: https://twitter.com/Docker\nLinkedIn: https://www.linkedin.com/company/docker/\nFacebook: https://www.facebook.com/docker.run\n\n--","viewCount":2473,"lengthSeconds":651,"watchProgress":305.822402,"timeWatched":1686902112828,"isLive":false,"paid":false,"type":"video","_id":"a9MWUiBI6zYh77yp"}
