{"videoId":"UHyVHHG8sw0","title":"This Makes Anatomy 10x Easier (no exaggeration)","author":"Love Life Drawing","authorId":"UCA9o111IH1VD8Kxz0YLn8_A","published":1672873200000,"description":"We will run the Fresh Eyes challenge live from 16th January in our community. It’s very powerful (and free!). Sign up to our community and get our super useful newsletter too: https://www.lovelifedrawing.com/fresheyes/\n\nJoin our community and access our free references: https://www.lovelifedrawing.com/figure-drawing-references/\n\nLearn about the Life Drawing Study Group: https://community.lovelifedrawing.com/the-life-drawing-study-group\n\nGet our free guide to life drawing skills and join our super useful newsletter: https://community.lovelifedrawing.com/checklist\n\nOverview for gesture: The 11 Steps to Great Gesture Drawing\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=NAY5N76VP8M\n\nLearn to see the ribcage: The MOST useful anatomy idea is also super simple\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jH0Vkkc3Mgw\n\nThis video is all about the pelvis! So important to figure drawing, but also quite a complicated shape. The anatomy police are going to arrest me for this one! We are going to bypass all the complexity of the pelvis and just take some easy ideas that still give us most of the drawing benefits.\n\nAnatomeasy is a series of tutorials I'm starting about the anatomy of different areas of the figure. A lot of the wonderful books and guidance out there about anatomy for artists is comprehensive and therefore quite complex! That's a hard place to start. So I want to help you get started by seeing the things that really matter the most.\n\n0:00 The 80/20 rule\n1:36 Find the angle of the pelvis\n5:44 Check the tilt\n7:17 Check the rotation to your eyes\n8:15 Remember the pelvis is a rigid mass\n11:12 See the whole story\n12:18 Extra quick tips","viewCount":6716,"lengthSeconds":886,"watchProgress":478.667879,"timeWatched":1673083678196,"isLive":false,"paid":false,"type":"video","_id":"aOTBnhIJl6oJOy1X"}
